vity of antioxidant transcription factors. During initiation, genetic changes enable cell survival under high ROS levels by activating antioxidant transcription factors or increasing NADPH via the pentose phosphate pathway (PPP). During progression and metastasis, tumor cells adapt to oxidative stress by increasing NADPH in various ways, including activation of AMPK, the PPP, and reductive glutamine and folate metabolism.", "affiliation": "Division of Cellular Medicine, Jacqui Wood Cancer Centre, Ninewells Hospital and Medical School, University of Dundee, Dundee DD1 9SY, UK, Scotland. Electronic address: j.d.hayes@dundee.ac.uk.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIGMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "GM", "grantId": "P20 GM103542", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Cancer Research UK", "acronym": "CRUK_", "grantId": "18644", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "South Carolina Center of Economic Excellence", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Cancer Research UK", "acronym": "CRUK_", "grantId": "C20953/A18644", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Medical Research Council", "acronym": "MRC_", "grantId": "MR/N009851/1", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Medical Research Council", "acronym": "MRC_", "grantId": "MR/T014644/1", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Medical Research Council", "acronym": "MRC_", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCRR NIH HHS", "acronym": "RR", "grantId": "C06 RR015455", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Cancer Research UK", "acronym": "CRUK_", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbre